        "text": "Know Your Trader (KYT) is a short, AI-conducted interview, separate from KYC identity checks, that confirms \"the person trading the account is the person who holds it.\" Under its KYT policy, Tradeify may require it before funding, before a payout or after a review, and says being asked \"is not an accusation of wrongdoing.\" Questions come from your own trading history, it usually takes under 10 minutes, and a Tradeify team member reviews every interview. You must answer yourself, without other people or AI tools. Missing the deadline can pause account activity, payouts or access."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use a VPN, VPS or a shared network with Tradeify?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You cannot log in through a VPN or VPS. Tradeify's Common FAQs say \"After logging in normally, you may use VPS for trading at your own risk.\" A shared household, network or device is not, by itself, a violation, according to its Risk & Compliance FAQ. Tradeify does use device, network and session data, and a review may follow when access looks designed to conceal ownership, operate others' accounts or evade limits, \"including through prohibited virtualization, remote-access, anonymization, or circumvention technologies.\" No single device or IP decides the outcome on its own."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I be long on one Tradeify account and short on another, or long ES and short NQ?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Tradeify's hedging rule bans opposing positions \"on the same instrument or on two products from the same Product Group,\" in one account or spread across your accounts. Long ES on one account and short NQ on another is a violation because both are Equity Index products, and contract size does not matter: long MES against short NQ is still a hedge. Opposite directions across different groups, such as long ES and short CL, are allowed. Every account involved can be set to violation status with profits forfeited, and deliberate or repeated cases can bring a permanent ban."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "I hedged for a few seconds by accident on Tradeify. Will my account be breached?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Not automatically, if you close it quickly. Tradeify's automated hedging check breaches an account only when all three conditions hold: opposing positions exist, \"The hedge duration exceeds 10 seconds,\" and profit from the hedge exceeds $150. Tradeify says the 10-second window lets a trader who opens an opposing position by mistake close it without penalty, and it \"is not an allowance to hold a hedge briefly on purpose.\" Cross-account and correlated-product hedges are reviewed separately by the risk team. If a platform error caused it, contact support immediately."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is copy trading allowed at Tradeify, and can I use a third-party copier?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, between accounts you own. Tradeify's Tradovate copy-trading guide says \"You may only group trade between accounts you own and manage,\" and copying other people's strategies or copy trading with others is not permitted. Third-party trade copiers are allowed \"at your own risk,\" and Tradeify does not support errors they cause. Copies must stay in the same direction: long ES on two of your accounts is fine, but opposite sides is a hedging violation. You can hold up to 5 funded accounts per household."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Tradeify's consistency rule work, and does it reset after a payout?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your biggest single day's profit must be at or below a set share of total profit before you can request a payout. Tradeify's consistency rule is 35% on Growth Sim Funded, 40% on Select Evaluations (none on Select funded accounts), and 20%, then 25%, then 30% by payout number on Lightning Funded accounts bought after September 12, 2025. Breaking it does not fail the account; you keep trading until the ratio comes down. Tradeify says \"After an approved payout, the consistency % will reset.\" The check is biggest day divided by total profit."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Tradeify's drawdown end-of-day or intraday, and when does it lock?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "All Tradeify accounts (Growth, Select and Lightning) use end-of-day trailing drawdown, but it is enforced in real time. The limit only updates at the close, yet if your net liquidation value touches it at any moment, the account fails, and recovering later that day does not undo it. On Sim Funded accounts (not evaluations), the drawdown locks once you profit beyond the drawdown amount by $100, or when you request a payout, whichever comes first. A 50K account locks at a $50,100 floor when its EOD balance reaches $52,100."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long do Tradeify payouts take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tradeify's Growth Funded payout policy says payments \"will be issued within 24-48 hours after the withdrawal has been processed,\" and requests submitted outside business hours (Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. EST, plus federal holidays) may take up to 72 hours. Payouts go through Rise, with Plane as an alternative, and per its Common FAQs you complete KYC with Rise when you first request one. Only one payout request can be open per account at a time. Traders receive 90% of the amount requested."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I hold positions overnight at Tradeify, and when do I have to be flat?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No overnight holds. Tradeify's Common FAQs answer \"Can I hold positions overnight?\" with \"No, you cannot,\" and say \"All positions must be closed before 4:45PM EST.\" A trading day runs from 6:00 PM to 5:00 PM EST/EDT the next day, and weekend trading is not allowed. News trading is allowed with no restrictions at Tradeify. CME exchange halts are not compensated, since they affect all market participants equally."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>

